          "content": "## Laboratory activities\n\n**Laboratory 1: Phase Relations Explorer.** Three-phase solids/water/air and derived state quantities. First predict the direction of change for the output when one control changes. Hold all other controls fixed; record a baseline, two variations, and a short discussion of why the governing assumptions are or are not credible. Navigate to `../labs/lab-01.html`. **Important:** Ideal phases; grain specific gravity and porosity are treated as known.\n\n**Laboratory 2: Plasticity State Map.** Atterberg limits and consistency index. First predict the direction of change for the output when one control changes. Hold all other controls fixed; record a baseline, two variations, and a short discussion of why the governing assumptions are or are not credible. Navigate to `../labs/lab-02.html`. **Important:** Index-based classification visualization; not an independent strength prediction."
