          "content": "## Laboratory activities\n\n**Laboratory 9: Mohr\u2013Coulomb Direct Shear.** Peak strength envelope and pore-pressure sensitivity. First predict the direction of change for the output when one control changes. Hold all other controls fixed; record a baseline, two variations, and a short discussion of why the governing assumptions are or are not credible. Navigate to `../labs/lab-09.html`. **Important:** Linear c\u2032\u2013\u03c6\u2032 fit at a selected effective normal stress.\n\n**Laboratory 10: Triaxial Stress Path.** Stress invariants and pore-pressure effect. First predict the direction of change for the output when one control changes. Hold all other controls fixed; record a baseline, two variations, and a short discussion of why the governing assumptions are or are not credible. Navigate to `../labs/lab-10.html`. **Important:** Axisymmetric triaxial compression state; no automatic failure criterion."
