          "heading": "Laboratory activities",
          "content": "## Laboratory activities\n\n**Laboratory 13: Infinite-Slope Stability.** Shear versus effective normal resistance in a shallow planar slope. First predict the direction of change for the output when one control changes. Hold all other controls fixed; record a baseline, two variations, and a short discussion of why the governing assumptions are or are not credible. Navigate to `../labs/lab-13.html`. **Important:** Uniform infinite slope with failure plane parallel to ground surface.\n\n**Laboratory 14: Simplified Strip Bearing Capacity.** Classical \u03c6=0 strip-footing benchmark. First predict the direction of change for the output when one control changes. Hold all other controls fixed; record a baseline, two variations, and a short discussion of why the governing assumptions are or are not credible. Navigate to `../labs/lab-14.html`. **Important:** Undrained homogeneous \u03c6=0 classroom idealization; no allowable pressure."
